1
00:00:07,299 --> 00:00:10,539
It's December 2000.

2
00:00:11,240 --> 00:00:13,490
Three Doors Down just gave us Kryptonite.

3
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:17,960
If I go crazy then will you still call me Superman?

4
00:00:18,679 --> 00:00:24,280
And Destiny's Child asked us to say my name, say my name, no one is around you.

5
00:00:24,460 --> 00:00:30,719
The Rams have won the Super Bowl for the first time since 1951 and X-Men the movie is released,

6
00:00:31,039 --> 00:00:35,259
showing Hollywood that big budget superhero films can be real cash cows.

7
00:00:36,079 --> 00:00:38,979
Y2K has come and gone without causing the world to collapse,

8
00:00:39,520 --> 00:00:43,659
though September of the next year would seem to do so, at least for us Americans.

9
00:00:44,500 --> 00:00:48,020
But in that short period we were in a sort of liminal space,

10
00:00:48,380 --> 00:00:50,820
a blissful innocence riding off the Clinton era.

11
00:00:51,659 --> 00:00:54,049
It was a new millennia, filled with new possibilities,

12
00:00:54,460 --> 00:00:57,119
and a recently turned 11 year old meromorphic.

13
00:00:58,159 --> 00:01:04,420
It's December 2000 and I'm with my father on our weekly trip to eat at Boston Market and then to

14
00:01:04,420 --> 00:01:08,799
either peruse the books at Barnes and Noble or the electronic toys at Fry's.

15
00:01:09,540 --> 00:01:14,760
We chose Fry's that week, first performing our ritual of checking what the largest hard drive was on sale.

16
00:01:15,180 --> 00:01:17,159
The capacities had been booming at the time.

17
00:01:17,500 --> 00:01:19,959
It seemed like it doubled every time we went in.

18
00:01:25,219 --> 00:01:32,959
On this day I found a game for my brand new PlayStation that my parents had bought me for my birthday family, Final Fantasy 8.

19
00:01:33,760 --> 00:01:39,659
It was immediately intriguing because it was in a thicker package, dick joke, said by the other PlayStation games,

20
00:01:49,140 --> 00:01:51,519
I don't really know why I chose that game.

21
00:01:51,920 --> 00:01:55,349
I knew nothing about it and I had no experience with JRPGs,

22
00:01:56,159 --> 00:01:58,040
not that I even knew what that term meant.

23
00:01:58,579 --> 00:02:01,879
Still, I bought it, or well my dad did,

24
00:02:02,560 --> 00:02:06,620
but regardless, I was engrossed from the very first cutscene.

25
00:02:11,659 --> 00:02:13,240
It's March 2001.

26
00:02:14,139 --> 00:02:20,300
Over three months later and I'm still playing this game and combing through every detail of the guidebook that I bought with it.

27
00:02:20,780 --> 00:02:23,780
The thing was rough and torn up as if from years of use,

28
00:02:24,060 --> 00:02:28,080
from me constantly flipping back and forth between the bestiary and weapons guides,

29
00:02:28,460 --> 00:02:33,819
constantly trying to eke out every little bit of an advantage to beat some of the harder optional bosses.

30
00:02:34,719 --> 00:02:38,319
All the while my mother's 40th birthday party is going on in the room next door.

31
00:02:39,039 --> 00:02:41,759
Her friends from high school had arranged a male stripper to come,

32
00:02:42,180 --> 00:02:46,400
and yet I was blissfully unaware, laser focused on my video game.

33
00:02:46,960 --> 00:02:50,879
My mother's friend said something like, everything is bigger in Texas?

34
00:02:51,800 --> 00:02:53,060
I focused harder on the game.

35
00:02:53,620 --> 00:02:54,060
I love you mom.

36
00:02:54,159 --> 00:02:56,580
So, I have a confession to make.

37
00:02:57,180 --> 00:02:59,560
I never beat the game on that first playthrough.

38
00:03:00,080 --> 00:03:07,240
But, but, since then I have gone back to play and complete Final Fantasy more times than any other game.

39
00:03:07,680 --> 00:03:10,620
I love absolutely everything about it.

40
00:03:11,000 --> 00:03:13,259
It has this intangible charm to me.

41
00:03:13,520 --> 00:03:17,120
Even the things that other people despise are some of my favorite parts.

42
00:03:17,879 --> 00:03:23,439
It was the first game that I had played that allowed me to completely strategize every encounter,

43
00:03:23,759 --> 00:03:27,020
building up my team and methodically taking down bosses.

44
00:03:27,319 --> 00:03:32,159
Hell, I even made an entire damn ass guide to beating one of those optional bosses.

45
00:03:32,439 --> 00:03:35,819
Which, I could have sworn I posted to GameFAQs.

46
00:03:36,919 --> 00:03:37,639
Where the hell are you?

47
00:03:38,069 --> 00:03:40,099
But, it seems lost to time.

48
00:03:40,919 --> 00:03:46,280
I start with all this because I need you to understand how much this game means to me,

49
00:03:46,780 --> 00:03:53,439
and as intangible, as ethereal as its charm is, I want to finally try to translate that.

50
00:03:54,060 --> 00:03:58,180
There is no possible way for me to be unbiased with this game,

51
00:03:58,560 --> 00:04:00,520
and so I'm not even going to try to fight it.

52
00:04:01,199 --> 00:04:03,400
This is not a normal retrospective.

53
00:04:03,979 --> 00:04:08,699
This is just a love letter to the game that first got me interested in gaming,

54
00:04:09,080 --> 00:04:11,280
that revealed I was a bit of a weeb,

55
00:04:11,580 --> 00:04:15,560
and that may have awakened strange tingly feelings for a certain character.

56
00:04:16,420 --> 00:04:19,199
This is a love letter to Final Fantasy VIII.

57
00:04:42,810 --> 00:04:46,689
Now, before we go any further, I need to make a second confession.

58
00:04:47,620 --> 00:04:51,459
I have never played Final Fantasy VII, at least not the original,

59
00:04:51,879 --> 00:04:53,540
and I may get flack for saying that I have never played Final Fantasy VII.

60
00:04:53,560 --> 00:04:58,339
I have played this, but I didn't like the remake at all, outside of the battle system.

61
00:04:58,980 --> 00:05:04,959
The mainline Final Fantasy games I have played are VIII, X, X, XII, XIII, and XV,

62
00:05:05,660 --> 00:05:07,360
so that's my experience with the series.

63
00:05:08,240 --> 00:05:08,540
We good?

64
00:05:09,180 --> 00:05:09,779
Okay, good.

65
00:05:10,399 --> 00:05:13,379
Final Fantasy VIII was first released in 1999,

66
00:05:13,939 --> 00:05:18,660
and the footage you're seeing on screen is from that original release, running through an emulator.

67
00:05:19,300 --> 00:05:23,160
Though the developer Square Enix had cut their teeth in 3D graphics

68
00:05:23,480 --> 00:05:27,959
with VII, VIII was notable in that the people were actually people-shaped,

69
00:05:28,300 --> 00:05:29,779
and not just ball and stick figures.

70
00:05:30,620 --> 00:05:33,379
This was already pretty mind-blowing to me at the time,

71
00:05:33,759 --> 00:05:39,319
but even more impressive were the full motion graphic cutscenes interspersed throughout the game,

72
00:05:39,740 --> 00:05:43,069
which were absolutely jaw-dropping for a game in 1999,

73
00:05:43,639 --> 00:05:50,139
especially considering that some of them were happening in the background while you controlled the normally rendered characters.

74
00:05:50,779 --> 00:05:54,319
To this day, seeing those scenes sends chills up my spine.

75
00:05:54,759 --> 00:06:04,060
The game was the brainchild of Yoshinori Kitase, who also directed many other games in the Final Fantasy series,

76
00:06:04,319 --> 00:06:09,579
notably VII and X, as well as Tetsuya Nomura, who was the character, monster,

77
00:06:09,839 --> 00:06:14,980
and battle system designer, and Yusuke Neoi, in charge of the FMV and backgrounds.

78
00:06:15,860 --> 00:06:20,220
The three built a world from the base theme of flipping VII on its head,

79
00:06:20,660 --> 00:06:27,060
as Neoi said in an interview, the previous Final Fantasy game had images of light emerging from darkness.

80
00:06:27,620 --> 00:06:31,480
It was very beautiful, but this time we decided to turn it upside down.

81
00:06:32,040 --> 00:06:32,980
Shadows in light.

82
00:06:33,480 --> 00:06:36,199
And at this, they hit the nail on the head.

83
00:06:36,779 --> 00:06:39,379
Throughout the entire game, there are little hints of darkness.

84
00:06:39,959 --> 00:06:44,519
As you move around the garden in the first two discs, you run into these mysterious figures,

85
00:06:44,839 --> 00:06:50,399
who slowly move more and more into the foreground, becoming these faceless symbols of authority.

86
00:06:50,939 --> 00:06:51,720
But whose authority?

87
00:06:52,459 --> 00:06:52,720
It's unclear.

88
00:06:53,560 --> 00:06:58,680
And right as you're really starting to question it, they cause a civil war between factions of the students.

89
00:06:59,319 --> 00:07:00,680
And that's just one example.

90
00:07:01,120 --> 00:07:05,720
The bright colors, the peppy music, and the funny character dialogue between Zell and Cypher,

91
00:07:06,480 --> 00:07:11,540
or the inherent silliness of Selfie being so ditzy despite being a professional mercenary,

92
00:07:11,879 --> 00:07:17,459
are all masks that the world of Final Fantasy VIII wears, concealing something darker.

93
00:07:18,019 --> 00:07:22,180
This speaks to me because it's a near-perfect reflection of our world.

94
00:07:22,639 --> 00:07:24,839
You know, minus the magic and the monsters,

95
00:07:25,100 --> 00:07:25,720
and yeah.

96
00:07:26,060 --> 00:07:31,740
It grounds the characters in a more relatable setting than really any of the other Final Fantasy games I've played,

97
00:07:31,980 --> 00:07:33,540
outside of maybe XV.

98
00:07:33,980 --> 00:07:35,420
But, whoa now.

99
00:07:35,699 --> 00:07:37,420
I'm getting ahead of myself.

100
00:07:37,879 --> 00:07:40,139
Who are Zell and Cypher and Selfie?

101
00:07:40,720 --> 00:07:41,620
What's a garden?

102
00:07:42,240 --> 00:07:44,019
What is Final Fantasy about?

103
00:07:44,439 --> 00:07:47,279
Well, let's do a brief synopsis.

104
00:07:47,980 --> 00:07:52,160
Bearing in mind that this is four discs worth of story, so brief is a relic.

105
00:07:53,560 --> 00:07:53,899
Oh lord.

106
00:07:54,519 --> 00:07:54,879
Here we go.

107
00:08:07,860 --> 00:08:10,759
You play as Squall, a lonely, brooding,

108
00:08:11,000 --> 00:08:14,500
hot-boy anime man who just wants to be left to his own devices.

109
00:08:14,959 --> 00:08:19,800
The game begins on a cutscene, showing a duel between Squall and his arch-nemesis, Cypher,

110
00:08:20,199 --> 00:08:21,180
who gets a strike on our boy, leaving a squall in the middle of the game.

111
00:08:22,870 --> 00:08:25,139
They each carry a gun blade.

112
00:08:25,420 --> 00:08:26,879
It's like a gun...

113
00:08:28,480 --> 00:08:28,920
with a blade.

114
00:08:29,040 --> 00:08:31,519
Completely impractical, yet totally awesome.

115
00:08:32,399 --> 00:08:36,320
Squall is a young mercenary in training for an organization called SEED.

116
00:08:36,860 --> 00:08:43,580
SEED operates throughout the world, taking on missions and training students in gardens, these giant school complexes.

117
00:08:44,519 --> 00:08:50,940
The game follows Squall's development as he first graduates the SEED exam by helping to liberate the nation of Dalit

118
00:08:50,940 --> 00:08:54,480
from a Galbadians, another nation hell-bent on world domination.

119
00:08:55,320 --> 00:09:00,639
Throughout the story, Squall gains companions, and the story becomes just as much theirs as it is his,

120
00:09:01,139 --> 00:09:03,500
each one being fleshed out, dynamic characters.

121
00:09:04,139 --> 00:09:06,639
The first of which is Squall's instructor, Quistus,

122
00:09:06,919 --> 00:09:10,700
who accompanies him on a makeup exam that he missed because of the duel with Cypher.

123
00:09:11,100 --> 00:09:16,460
Here, Squall gets his first, or if you're attentive, third, GF.

124
00:09:17,139 --> 00:09:23,039
Guardian forces are basically friendly monsters that you can assign or junction to your characters.

125
00:09:23,919 --> 00:09:26,259
They can be summoned in a battle to attack the enemy,

126
00:09:26,440 --> 00:09:29,179
but have tons of other uses that we'll get into later.

127
00:09:29,919 --> 00:09:36,860
You get a bunch of these Guardian forces throughout the game either by fighting them directly or by drawing them from other enemies.

128
00:09:38,200 --> 00:09:40,080
Quistus is only a year older than Squall,

129
00:09:40,379 --> 00:09:42,559
but is clearly much wiser than he is.

130
00:09:42,860 --> 00:09:49,500
She sees right through Squall's brooding bad boy act and constantly shows it by literally finishing his sentences before he can.

131
00:09:50,559 --> 00:09:54,500
Next is Zell, who can be summed up in a single word, volatile.

132
00:09:55,299 --> 00:10:01,620
He is extremely loyal, but press the right buttons and he flies off in a rage, which Cypher does constantly.

133
00:10:02,500 --> 00:10:03,919
The fourth member is Selfie.

134
00:10:04,320 --> 00:10:09,620
We first meet her on Squall's seed exam, where she joins the party after Cypher goes off by himself.

135
00:10:10,220 --> 00:10:12,139
Selfie is a walking contradiction.

136
00:10:12,720 --> 00:10:17,539
She is a mercenary in training, yet she is also clumsy and completely innocent.

137
00:10:18,120 --> 00:10:21,320
She's deadly, but more likely to hug you than hit you.

138
00:10:22,240 --> 00:10:27,440
After passing the exam, Squall and the other newly promoted seeds are treated to a celebration ball,

139
00:10:27,740 --> 00:10:31,240
where we meet the fifth member of Squall Team 6, Rinoa.

140
00:10:31,820 --> 00:10:36,960
She is the main love interest in the game, and she immediately has Squall's number, just like Quistus,

141
00:10:37,240 --> 00:10:41,720
constantly teasing him, prying his feelings out, even if it's just an angry reaction.

142
00:10:42,360 --> 00:10:46,120
There's this half-hearted attempt at a love triangle here with Cypher,

143
00:10:46,220 --> 00:10:51,559
but it never really materializes and it's always clear that Rinoa and Squall are going to end up together.

144
00:10:52,220 --> 00:10:53,440
So I'm just going to ignore it.

145
00:10:54,139 --> 00:10:55,779
As quickly as it began, the dance ends,

146
00:10:56,419 --> 00:11:02,320
and Squall is on his first seed mission to help a small resistance movement liberate the nation of Timber

147
00:11:02,700 --> 00:11:03,840
from Galbadian control.

148
00:11:04,399 --> 00:11:06,620
Galbadia just has their grubby fingers and everything.

149
00:11:07,600 --> 00:11:11,100
That small resistance is led by none other than Rinoa.

150
00:11:11,879 --> 00:11:17,039
During their mission, there's this awesome FMV sequence with our characters running across a moving train,

151
00:11:17,600 --> 00:11:20,879
and then a section that I failed so many times as a child,

152
00:11:21,179 --> 00:11:24,799
I still have PTSD from it and save scum like crazy when I get there.

153
00:11:25,639 --> 00:11:28,440
Side note, there are a lot of trains in this game.

154
00:11:28,700 --> 00:11:34,500
Seriously, if that Tumblr blog raiding Marvel movies by the number of trains in them did the same thing with

155
00:11:34,500 --> 00:11:37,860
the Final Fantasy series, 8 would be at the tippy top.

156
00:11:38,399 --> 00:11:41,440
Seriously, even one of the Guardian forces is a train.

157
00:11:42,559 --> 00:11:46,700
But the plan, which was to capture the Galbadian president, goes tits up

158
00:11:47,039 --> 00:11:51,639
when it's revealed that the president on the train was actually a body double monster.

159
00:11:52,240 --> 00:11:55,820
They defeat it, but now Galbadia is in on what's going on.

160
00:11:56,360 --> 00:12:01,100
It's revealed here that the reason GBADs wanted Dalit, the place you freed in the seed exam,

161
00:12:01,419 --> 00:12:03,779
was to get access to their communications tower.

162
00:12:04,240 --> 00:12:09,539
Apparently, long-range radio broadcasts haven't been a thing for nearly 20 years in this world,

163
00:12:09,580 --> 00:12:12,860
and so they revived the tower to send out an important message.

164
00:12:13,500 --> 00:12:19,379
That message was to announce the new Galbadian ambassador, the real power behind the government,

165
00:12:19,919 --> 00:12:23,100
the sorceress Edea and her knight, Cypher.

166
00:12:25,409 --> 00:12:30,580
After failing to stop the broadcast and being brushed aside in their first encounter with Edea,

167
00:12:30,860 --> 00:12:36,960
Squall's crew are forced to flee Timber for Galbadia Garden, which is supposedly unaffiliated with the country of its namesake.

168
00:12:37,519 --> 00:12:42,860
There, they are immediately drafted into a mission to assassinate sorceress Edea.

169
00:12:43,320 --> 00:12:47,740
It is here that we meet the final member of the squad, Irvine Keneas.

170
00:12:48,480 --> 00:12:51,100
He is a sniper, supposedly a lone wolf character,

171
00:12:51,700 --> 00:12:56,860
but is, in reality, much more outgoing than Squall and generally nicer than Zell.

172
00:12:57,480 --> 00:13:03,879
Their inside man in Galbadia's capital city is a high-ranking general who is revealed to be Rinoa's father.

173
00:13:04,320 --> 00:13:05,240
Some hijinks occur.

174
00:13:05,600 --> 00:13:07,340
Rinoa gets temporarily captured.

175
00:13:07,720 --> 00:13:12,980
Irvine's sniper shot is deflected by a barrier sorceress Edea puts up at the last second,

176
00:13:13,340 --> 00:13:16,919
and so Squall is forced to rush in and attack her head-on.

177
00:13:17,240 --> 00:13:24,419
They do battle, but Edea is ultimately victorious, and before leaving, she shoots an icicle through Squall's shoulder.

178
00:13:25,159 --> 00:13:26,659
Cue the end of disc one.

179
00:13:27,840 --> 00:13:29,960
Oh, Christ, there are three more of these to cover?

180
00:13:30,500 --> 00:13:32,559
Okay, so Laguna from the dream sequences.

181
00:13:33,429 --> 00:13:35,179
Shit, I forgot to mention the dream sequences.

182
00:13:35,980 --> 00:13:37,320
This shit is all falling apart.

183
00:13:37,500 --> 00:13:41,340
So a few times throughout the game, Squall and the others randomly pass out,

184
00:13:41,620 --> 00:13:43,019
and they wake up as other people.

185
00:13:43,320 --> 00:13:44,980
Laguna, Kuros, and Ward.

186
00:13:45,320 --> 00:13:47,100
They aren't really controlling these people,

187
00:13:47,259 --> 00:13:51,759
they just witness the events and are able to read the thoughts of the people they're inhabiting.

188
00:13:52,539 --> 00:13:54,700
Don't worry if you're confused, that's natural.

189
00:13:55,059 --> 00:14:00,100
Give it about five minutes for me to explain, and if your confusion still hasn't gone down, cast Isuna.

190
00:14:01,970 --> 00:14:04,779
So disc two begins with the Laguna sequence.

191
00:14:05,440 --> 00:14:07,519
He's living in a small town called Windhill.

192
00:14:08,379 --> 00:14:08,970
Who is Laguna?

193
00:14:09,139 --> 00:14:12,279
Well, he's a retired Galbadian soldier, but a good one.

194
00:14:12,759 --> 00:14:16,039
He's living with a woman named Rain and a little girl named Alone,

195
00:14:16,440 --> 00:14:18,000
and he's helping out around the town.

196
00:14:18,659 --> 00:14:19,460
Remember those names.

197
00:14:20,200 --> 00:14:24,379
Squall and the gang eventually wake up, finding themselves in a Galbadian prison,

198
00:14:24,639 --> 00:14:29,200
with Squall being tortured by Cipher, asking what Seed's true purpose is.

199
00:14:29,820 --> 00:14:35,299
We get our first clues that the dream sequences actually happened in the past and weren't just something that they're

200
00:14:35,299 --> 00:14:40,539
imagining, as Zell realizes that he knows the prison layout from living inside Ward,

201
00:14:40,940 --> 00:14:46,580
and some of the little Moogle monsters keep saying Laguna to Squall, and even assist their escape.

202
00:14:47,360 --> 00:14:48,559
Cue a prison break scene,

203
00:14:48,600 --> 00:14:55,539
and the realization that the whole complex is made up of three giant screws that can submerge the prison underground

204
00:14:55,539 --> 00:14:56,860
in the middle of a desert.

205
00:14:57,360 --> 00:14:57,860
Fucking awesome.

206
00:14:58,580 --> 00:15:00,220
At this point, the group splits up,

207
00:15:00,419 --> 00:15:07,860
because news has spread that the Galbadians were targeting the Gardens with missiles for their involvement in the assassination attempt on the sorceress.

208
00:15:08,440 --> 00:15:14,440
As they decide what to do, missiles are already launched for Trabia Guard, Selfie's original home.

209
00:15:15,340 --> 00:15:18,600
Selfie goes on a mission to shut down the missile base to prevent the strikes,

210
00:15:18,960 --> 00:15:22,879
while Squall leads a team to Balam Garden, their home, to evacuate.

211
00:15:23,639 --> 00:15:28,679
Selfie is successful in destroying the base, but it appears that her team is killed by the explosion.

212
00:15:29,240 --> 00:15:31,179
Squall's team, on the other hand, what's that?

213
00:15:32,379 --> 00:15:33,080
You hear that?

214
00:15:33,539 --> 00:15:36,379
The plot is going off the rails!

215
00:15:38,679 --> 00:15:41,860
Squall returns to the Garden to find it in the midst of a civil war.

216
00:15:42,159 --> 00:15:46,960
Apparently, there are two factions, the Headmaster Cid and Garden Master Norg.

217
00:15:47,419 --> 00:15:49,879
Up until now, we've never really heard of the latter,

218
00:15:50,360 --> 00:15:55,960
but we have seen his minions skulking about in the background, occasionally giving orders of reprimands.

219
00:15:56,259 --> 00:16:01,820
It turns out that Norg wants to give up Squall's crew to the sorceress in order to gain clemency for

220
00:16:01,820 --> 00:16:04,519
the assassination, but that just won't do.

221
00:16:05,139 --> 00:16:09,820
We also learn here that the Headmaster, Cid, is actually married to Edea,

222
00:16:10,139 --> 00:16:14,620
and that Cid was founded to fight the sorceress, should the need arise.

223
00:16:15,259 --> 00:16:21,820
So Squall defeats Norg and activates some mysterious machinery in the bowels of the Garden, and holy fucking crap,

224
00:16:21,960 --> 00:16:22,960
the Garden is a giant ship.

225
00:16:23,799 --> 00:16:26,500
The Garden is a giant fucking ship.

226
00:16:27,100 --> 00:16:31,820
My 11-year-old brain broke at this point when I first played the game.

227
00:16:33,100 --> 00:16:33,360
So awesome.

228
00:16:34,480 --> 00:16:37,179
The ship gains mobility and a disaster is averted.

229
00:16:37,559 --> 00:16:40,539
In the middle of all the action between Cid and Norg,

230
00:16:40,740 --> 00:16:44,580
a mysterious ship appears to whisk away a girl named Lone.

231
00:16:45,220 --> 00:16:45,759
Remember that name?

232
00:16:46,000 --> 00:16:49,559
Well, she was also the one who checked on Squall at the beginning of the game.

233
00:16:49,559 --> 00:16:53,059
She reveals that she was the one sending the gang into the game.

234
00:16:53,100 --> 00:16:53,799
the dream world.

235
00:16:54,720 --> 00:16:56,840
Though we don't learn everything at this point.

236
00:16:57,759 --> 00:17:02,820
Without navigation, however, the Garden eventually drifts into a floating town out in the ocean,

237
00:17:03,100 --> 00:17:05,859
nearly crushing a fisherman and the rest of its inhabitants.

238
00:17:06,680 --> 00:17:11,099
Here too, Galbadia is invading, trying to find Lone for some reason.

239
00:17:11,759 --> 00:17:16,480
After a boss battle, it's revealed that Selfie's team survived the missile base explosion,

240
00:17:16,779 --> 00:17:20,920
and the Screw, that's Squall's crew, is reunited.

241
00:17:21,759 --> 00:17:25,279
As the ship is prepared, the Screw, and the Screw, okay, I'm done using that term,

242
00:17:25,759 --> 00:17:28,900
Squall's crew set up a concert to cheer up their leader,

243
00:17:29,319 --> 00:17:31,599
and Squall and Rinoa get some alone time.

244
00:17:32,359 --> 00:17:36,000
And we get this awesome concert scene.

245
00:17:36,680 --> 00:17:42,059
So once the Garden is pilotable, the gang visits Trabia Garden, Selfie's original school,

246
00:17:42,480 --> 00:17:45,140
only to find it devastated by the Galbadian missiles.

247
00:17:45,519 --> 00:17:51,940
Fortunately, there were survivors, and it is here on the basketball courts where the story breaks wide open.

248
00:17:52,380 --> 00:17:58,440
Irvine recalls his time living in an orphanage as a child, with other kids, and a woman named Matrone.

249
00:17:58,900 --> 00:18:05,400
Quickly, the others all realized that, except for Rinoa, they were all living in that same orphanage,

250
00:18:05,500 --> 00:18:09,779
and that Matrone was their name for Edea, the orphanage mother.

251
00:18:10,519 --> 00:18:16,519
The reason that none of them remembered up until this trigger was due to the Guardian forces, or GFs.

252
00:18:16,819 --> 00:18:21,400
Apparently, junctioning them takes up a spot in the brain linked to memories,

253
00:18:21,980 --> 00:18:24,799
and so the more they are junctioned, the more memories are lost.

254
00:18:25,440 --> 00:18:27,880
Memories. History lost for power.

255
00:18:28,500 --> 00:18:29,339
Interesting concept.

256
00:18:29,700 --> 00:18:32,160
It was never mentioned before this point as being a possibility,

257
00:18:32,440 --> 00:18:34,180
but sure, we'll roll with it.

258
00:18:34,640 --> 00:18:41,079
After the Epiphany, the team decides to visit the orphanage, but are thwarted by the also-mobile Galbadia Garden.

259
00:18:41,380 --> 00:18:42,140
It's a ship, too.

260
00:18:42,819 --> 00:18:46,019
A standoff begins above the forest on the Cintra continent,

261
00:18:46,579 --> 00:18:48,460
between two floating behemoths.

262
00:18:48,599 --> 00:18:51,079
A huge battle between the mobile gardens

263
00:18:51,079 --> 00:18:54,920
and and squall, and Squall and Rinoa take the fight to Galbadia Garden,

264
00:18:55,220 --> 00:18:58,900
and face off with sorceress Edea and Cipher for a second time.

265
00:18:59,460 --> 00:19:01,279
This time, though, they are victorious.

266
00:19:01,799 --> 00:19:05,579
Edea is defeated, and suddenly has an abrupt personality change.

267
00:19:06,319 --> 00:19:06,599
Odd that.

268
00:19:07,220 --> 00:19:09,299
Meanwhile, Rinoa is in a trance.

269
00:19:09,559 --> 00:19:13,839
She moves around like a puppet, revives Cipher, and then goes into a coma.

270
00:19:14,559 --> 00:19:17,099
Weird. Thus ends Disc 2.

271
00:19:17,779 --> 00:19:19,359
Ok, let's pick up the pace a bit.

272
00:19:19,839 --> 00:19:23,440
Disc 3 is centered around around finding a way to revive Rinoa.

273
00:19:23,680 --> 00:19:27,420
Another major plot point is revealed here, probably the biggest one.

274
00:19:27,779 --> 00:19:30,180
Edea was not acting on her own accord,

275
00:19:30,440 --> 00:19:38,660
but was in fact being possessed by another sorceress from the future, Ultimesia, the ultimate big bad of the game.

276
00:19:39,059 --> 00:19:42,759
Edea tells Squall that Elone may be able to help Rinoa wake up,

277
00:19:43,059 --> 00:19:45,500
but upon finding the ship that she escaped on,

278
00:19:45,920 --> 00:19:51,359
Squall finds out that Elone escaped on another ship bound for the nation of Esthar.

279
00:19:51,799 --> 00:19:53,220
Yes, you heard that right.

280
00:19:53,440 --> 00:19:58,980
She left Balamgarden, which was at the time a ship, to hide on the White Siege ship,

281
00:19:59,400 --> 00:20:02,579
and then left that ship to jump on an Esthar ship.

282
00:20:02,799 --> 00:20:07,940
So Squall decides to set out on his own, carrying Rinoa on his back to find Elone in Esthar.

283
00:20:08,180 --> 00:20:10,019
Esthar. Esthar.

284
00:20:10,299 --> 00:20:15,660
To find Elone in Esthar, though of course the rest of the group can't be separated so easily.

285
00:20:16,140 --> 00:20:18,180
They intercept and join him on the way.

286
00:20:18,440 --> 00:20:23,660
And it's quite touching, because they really have built up this friendship over the course of the game.

287
00:20:24,240 --> 00:20:29,039
Esthar is a hidden country once ruled by another evil sorceress named Adele.

288
00:20:29,279 --> 00:20:30,119
Not that one.

289
00:20:30,339 --> 00:20:32,819
Though Laguna helped capture and imprison her.

290
00:20:33,319 --> 00:20:39,819
Up until this point, it's also been completely inaccessible as the continent is ringed by cliffs on all sides.

291
00:20:40,420 --> 00:20:43,440
And so you just couldn't get the garden up there because it needs a beach.

292
00:20:44,380 --> 00:20:49,200
But also, the city is ringed by an active, camouflage, protective barrier,

293
00:20:49,559 --> 00:20:51,779
and it's completely invisible from the outside.

294
00:20:52,200 --> 00:20:54,000
Still, the crew find a way in.

295
00:20:54,400 --> 00:20:55,259
There, Dr.

296
00:20:55,460 --> 00:20:58,119
Odine, this guy, agrees to help them,

297
00:20:58,240 --> 00:21:02,900
and sends up Squall and Rinoa to a lunar base to finally reunite with Elone.

298
00:21:03,240 --> 00:21:06,640
Unfortunately, this was all part of Ultimecia's plan.

299
00:21:06,960 --> 00:21:13,299
She had switched bodies in Disc 2 from Edea to Rinoa in that last fight, and once again,

300
00:21:13,519 --> 00:21:18,720
takes control of Rinoa in the lunar base to release the seals on sorceress Adele's prison.

301
00:21:18,980 --> 00:21:25,700
Adele was so powerful that their combined power, Adele and Ultimecia, would be nigh unstoppable.

302
00:21:26,019 --> 00:21:32,660
This is all coinciding with an event called the Lunar Cry, which isn't super relevant to the plot,

303
00:21:32,779 --> 00:21:34,240
but is really cool nonetheless.

304
00:21:34,799 --> 00:21:40,299
There's this really weird giant floating obelisk called the Lunatic Pandora or the Lunatic Pandora?

305
00:21:40,460 --> 00:21:41,119
Not sure.

306
00:21:41,259 --> 00:21:44,059
And when it floats over a spot called Tears Point,

307
00:21:44,440 --> 00:21:48,400
all this shit lights up and a funnel from the moon to the Earth is formed,

308
00:21:48,619 --> 00:21:52,140
allowing monsters to come to the Earth in like a giant wave.

309
00:21:52,640 --> 00:21:57,519
Yeah, apparently all the monsters on Earth came from the moon in vents like these.

310
00:21:57,900 --> 00:22:01,319
So who the fuck made this thing and why?

311
00:22:02,119 --> 00:22:08,700
Anyways, Adele is released from her prison and gets caught in the monster wave, crashing down inside the Lunatic Pandora.

312
00:22:09,160 --> 00:22:13,880
In order to release Adele, Rinoa, possessed by the spirit of Michael Rinoa.

313
00:22:14,660 --> 00:22:14,660
The two are saved by the moon.

314
00:22:15,059 --> 00:22:15,059
The two are saved by the moon in the moon.

315
00:22:15,059 --> 00:22:18,420
The moonwalk trance outside the lunar base to the prison, in space.

316
00:22:19,059 --> 00:22:23,339
When it was done, she was knocked into the void and was quickly running out of oxygen.

317
00:22:24,180 --> 00:22:28,819
Meanwhile, the base is breaking apart and everyone has to evacuate into pods.

318
00:22:29,259 --> 00:22:34,640
Squad, having walked across a continent to save Rinoa, wasn't about to let that fly, however,

319
00:22:35,140 --> 00:22:37,000
and so he dives into space after her.

320
00:22:37,720 --> 00:22:43,039
The two are saved by a literal deus ex machina in the form of a Ragnarok ship.

321
00:22:43,519 --> 00:22:46,839
An abandoned Esthar vessel that just happened to float by.

322
00:22:47,440 --> 00:22:53,319
After clearing the ship of its Ridley Scott inspired inhabitants, the two begin to make their way back to Earth,

323
00:22:53,779 --> 00:22:56,059
sharing a tender moment in the pilot seat.

324
00:22:56,640 --> 00:23:03,539
It wasn't meant to last though, because the Esthar air control informs them that Rinoa, being a sorceress now,

325
00:23:03,799 --> 00:23:09,599
will be taken into custody on their landing and sealed so that Ultimecia cannot take control of her again.

326
00:23:10,960 --> 00:23:14,619
For the time being, Rinoa and Squall accept this fate for her,

327
00:23:14,839 --> 00:23:20,539
but after letting her go and then talking to the rest of the team, Squall decides, hell with that,

328
00:23:20,660 --> 00:23:21,599
we're getting our girl back.

329
00:23:22,339 --> 00:23:23,200
And they do.

330
00:23:23,819 --> 00:23:26,319
They just get her back, literally just like that.

331
00:23:26,700 --> 00:23:30,339
It's honestly kind of weird how fast and quick about the turnabout is, but ultimately,

332
00:23:31,140 --> 00:23:35,099
after talking with Laguna, who is now the president of Esthar, apparently,

333
00:23:35,579 --> 00:23:38,680
they learn that Ultimecia is trying to compress time.

334
00:23:39,660 --> 00:23:42,720
So that she can rule in the past, present, and future.

335
00:23:43,200 --> 00:23:45,420
And she wants to do so using Elone.

336
00:23:45,900 --> 00:23:53,660
The group forms an admittedly opaque plan wherein they kill Adele and force Ultimecia to possess Rinoa,

337
00:23:54,019 --> 00:23:56,259
being the only other sorceress of the time.

338
00:23:56,759 --> 00:24:02,279
Elone then partially compresses time, halting it from doing so completely, I think,

339
00:24:02,960 --> 00:24:06,940
and sends Ultimecia back to her future castle where the gang is hot on her heels.

340
00:24:07,720 --> 00:24:12,880
Because Elone has this, like, time compression power, she can send consciousness back to her past.

341
00:24:13,380 --> 00:24:18,420
Yeah. After fighting their way through Ultimecia's castle, they finally confront the sorceress,

342
00:24:18,700 --> 00:24:26,299
and a grueling battle ensues, including Ultimecia's GF, Griever, which is the name Squall gave to his necklace pendant.

343
00:24:27,039 --> 00:24:29,920
I never really got this part, but according to the wiki,

344
00:24:30,500 --> 00:24:33,940
Griever is not only a symbol of the virtue Squall values,

345
00:24:34,539 --> 00:24:38,559
but is also Squall's interpretation of the ultimate guardian force.

346
00:24:39,180 --> 00:24:43,240
During the final battle, Ultimecia draws Griever from Squall's mind,

347
00:24:43,740 --> 00:24:47,579
bringing Squall's perception of the being into existence to fight the party.

348
00:24:48,000 --> 00:24:51,640
Apparently, this is made more explicit in the Japanese version, though.

349
00:24:52,160 --> 00:24:55,619
So, either way, they ultimately defeat Ultimecia.

350
00:24:56,220 --> 00:24:59,339
Finally victorious, the group are scattered across time,

351
00:24:59,720 --> 00:25:06,779
walking in a void with only their connections between one another as a guide to reinstate themselves in their proper times.

352
00:25:07,420 --> 00:25:12,200
We see Laguna at Rain's grave, Elone going to meet him and Squall looking on.

353
00:25:12,839 --> 00:25:17,740
We see a dying Ultimecia passing on her powers in the past to a young Edea,

354
00:25:18,160 --> 00:25:25,599
and finally we see Squall, lost and alone, passed out, possibly dead, finally found by Rinoa.

355
00:25:25,980 --> 00:25:29,119
The final scene shows a celebration at Balam Garden,

356
00:25:29,480 --> 00:25:34,400
with Rinoa on the balcony, and in the final moments, we see Squall embrace her.

357
00:25:34,660 --> 00:25:35,900
Apparently, he lived.

358
00:25:36,740 --> 00:25:37,119
Cut to black.

359
00:25:37,940 --> 00:25:38,799
Directed by Neil Druckmann.

360
00:25:48,839 --> 00:25:51,480
So, what did all this mean?

361
00:25:52,380 --> 00:25:59,140
The story, while all over the place at times, does successfully, in my opinion, tackle a lot of different topics.

362
00:25:59,880 --> 00:26:01,440
That's one thing I love about this game.

363
00:26:01,859 --> 00:26:05,380
The other is that humanity is dripping from every character.

364
00:26:05,940 --> 00:26:11,319
There's so much pathos and love between all of them by the end that you can't help but root for

365
00:26:11,319 --> 00:26:13,380
them to succeed, and to do so together.

366
00:26:14,380 --> 00:26:17,579
So many nice details and themes, so much to discuss,

367
00:26:18,339 --> 00:26:20,519
so I think I'll just point out some of the greatest hits.

368
00:26:21,480 --> 00:26:24,039
Like Squall learning to accept that he needs others.

369
00:26:24,579 --> 00:26:27,619
He was alone as a child, feeling abandoned by a loan,

370
00:26:27,920 --> 00:26:29,880
and so put up walls around himself.

371
00:26:30,380 --> 00:26:36,900
Only through his friends, and importantly not just Rinoa, but all of them, was he finally able to do so.

372
00:26:37,299 --> 00:26:43,559
His story ends as it begins, where at first he was alone and afraid, being abandoned, as he thought,

373
00:26:43,759 --> 00:26:44,400
by his sister.

374
00:26:44,900 --> 00:26:46,960
And at the end he is alone and afraid.

375
00:26:47,259 --> 00:26:50,599
Only this time he is saved by Rinoa, who refused to be saved by Rinoa,

376
00:26:50,599 --> 00:26:50,599
who refused to be saved by Rinoa.

377
00:26:50,640 --> 00:26:51,740
He refused to abandon him.

378
00:26:52,140 --> 00:26:56,880
This is his main character arc, and it's expressed perfectly through his actions,

379
00:26:57,359 --> 00:26:58,539
and even through gameplay.

380
00:26:59,140 --> 00:27:03,960
Every natural point where characters express their feelings, Squall goes quiet.

381
00:27:04,440 --> 00:27:11,019
He is also the most self-sufficient character in the game, having the highest base attack and hit percent stats.

382
00:27:11,619 --> 00:27:14,380
In other words, the game is telling you that he is a loner,

383
00:27:14,940 --> 00:27:17,799
though obviously he can't do everything on his own.

384
00:27:18,640 --> 00:27:19,680
Then there's Rinoa.

385
00:27:20,180 --> 00:27:26,460
In a super relatable way, for me especially, she feels this imposter syndrome creep up throughout the game.

386
00:27:26,940 --> 00:27:33,759
In the beginning, she is this super spunky, super confident rebel planning to capture a president of an invading nation.

387
00:27:34,240 --> 00:27:37,940
But as time goes on and the events get larger and larger in scope,

388
00:27:38,420 --> 00:27:44,240
she sees herself less as that rebel and more as the only non-seed in the group.

389
00:27:44,799 --> 00:27:50,519
She feels like she holds them back, despite the actual gameplay showing us that she holds her own,

390
00:27:50,720 --> 00:27:51,819
just as well as the others.

391
00:27:52,420 --> 00:27:57,960
This is so clear to the player that when she says it, our natural reaction is, say, what?

392
00:27:58,500 --> 00:27:59,710
I'm just a little confused.

393
00:28:00,579 --> 00:28:05,240
But that is good because imposter syndrome really doesn't make logical sense.

394
00:28:05,779 --> 00:28:10,000
And in the end, she accepts her role as both a member of Squall Team 6

395
00:28:10,460 --> 00:28:14,420
and a sorceress, helping in a big way to take down the big bad.

396
00:28:15,480 --> 00:28:18,000
Or even smaller details, like in the end,

397
00:28:18,160 --> 00:28:22,839
when Ultimecia goes to the past and passes on her powers to Edea.

398
00:28:23,299 --> 00:28:28,319
Squall watches on and even talks to Edea there, telling her that he is a seed,

399
00:28:28,779 --> 00:28:32,339
destined to fight the sorceress, Edea not knowing what the hell he's talking about.

400
00:28:33,119 --> 00:28:40,519
So then, later on, Edea creates seed and garden together with Cid, which trains Squall to fight the sorceress,

401
00:28:41,059 --> 00:28:45,299
eventually going back to tell Edea, who creates seed and garden together.

402
00:28:45,539 --> 00:28:46,339
Time travel is fucky.

403
00:28:46,680 --> 00:28:47,819
And it's a nice nod from the writers.

404
00:28:48,400 --> 00:28:52,000
Or the fact that Squall is clearly Laguna and Rain's kid.

405
00:28:52,420 --> 00:28:54,700
The game never really explicitly says it,

406
00:28:55,039 --> 00:29:00,940
but it can be gleaned from little dialogue about Rain dying in childbirth while Laguna is off to find a loan.

407
00:29:01,359 --> 00:29:03,680
Or the Moogles calling Squall Laguna.

408
00:29:04,160 --> 00:29:08,500
Rain dying and Laguna being off would have left Squall as an orphan,

409
00:29:08,740 --> 00:29:11,460
which is why he was sent to live with Matrone and the others.

410
00:29:12,160 --> 00:29:15,920
I mean, I guess that one's more like a fact than it is an awesome story point,

411
00:29:16,000 --> 00:29:17,440
but it is a fun fact nonetheless.

412
00:29:18,599 --> 00:29:23,000
There's just so much to love, so much to unpack with this story and its characters.

413
00:29:23,599 --> 00:29:25,420
The female characters, holy cow.

414
00:29:26,079 --> 00:29:32,000
They made young me realize that playing as a girl in a game was okay and even cool.

415
00:29:32,480 --> 00:29:35,200
That was a big revelation for 11 year old me.

416
00:29:35,799 --> 00:29:40,839
Interestingly, despite being made to look more realistic, even accounting for graphics,

417
00:29:41,299 --> 00:29:47,900
the women here aren't really hyper-sexualized like some characters in some other game.

418
00:29:49,359 --> 00:29:51,019
Quistis is absolutely amazing.

419
00:29:51,319 --> 00:29:55,700
Her ability to completely see through Squall from the very beginning is disarming.

420
00:29:55,960 --> 00:30:02,579
It's a nice touch where the game sort of pokes fun at itself for playing this very stereotypical stoic main protagonist.

421
00:30:03,160 --> 00:30:06,660
Her very presence makes early Squall feel like a better character.

422
00:30:07,220 --> 00:30:11,740
Not only that, she is really powerful in the gameplay with her many blue magic limit breaks,

423
00:30:12,359 --> 00:30:15,220
some of which can insta-kill any non-boss combatants.

424
00:30:16,059 --> 00:30:19,359
The world itself is filled with secrets and intrigue.

425
00:30:19,880 --> 00:30:27,000
Throughout the game, you hear of sorceresses, run across ancient relics and a huge unexplained crater in the north.

426
00:30:27,660 --> 00:30:33,299
There's so much history to this world and it feels like the game only ever really scratches the surface of it.

427
00:30:33,660 --> 00:30:36,720
We get to hear about things like the Sorceress War in Esthar,

428
00:30:37,180 --> 00:30:38,880
but where are the sorceresses from?

429
00:30:39,380 --> 00:30:44,279
What does the term sorceress mean when anybody trained can use magic spells?

430
00:30:44,920 --> 00:30:47,920
We get to hear that the gardens were once refugees from the world.

431
00:30:47,940 --> 00:30:49,539
shelters and that's why they can move.

432
00:30:49,900 --> 00:30:51,400
But refugees from what?

433
00:30:52,019 --> 00:30:52,839
We don't really know.

434
00:30:53,420 --> 00:30:57,039
What the hell is the lunatic Pandora beyond a monster summoning device?

435
00:30:57,440 --> 00:30:58,960
Who created it and why?

436
00:30:59,799 --> 00:31:02,700
So much, yet we only get to see the tiniest bit.

437
00:31:03,140 --> 00:31:05,220
But that's actually great for world building.

438
00:31:05,599 --> 00:31:08,859
It gives us a reason to go scour the continents for secrets,

439
00:31:09,059 --> 00:31:13,579
to find crazy powers or GF allies or find that tiny scrap.

440
00:31:14,380 --> 00:31:16,059
It gives us a reason to explore.

441
00:31:16,779 --> 00:31:19,440
I know this isn't technically an open world game.

442
00:31:19,779 --> 00:31:22,059
It's an overworld with levels built in.

443
00:31:22,640 --> 00:31:29,140
But I still feel like this was my first open world experience since it's so huge and full of mystery.

444
00:31:29,819 --> 00:31:36,799
Sorceresses, magic, space stations, hot boys and hot girls, flying fortresses doing battle, time travel.

445
00:31:37,039 --> 00:31:39,940
The game has all the action and show stopping elements,

446
00:31:40,299 --> 00:31:41,819
but it also has heart.

447
00:31:42,380 --> 00:31:43,960
It's seriousness and humanity.

448
00:31:44,599 --> 00:31:51,579
Final Fantasy VIII's has a lot to offer and these are the reasons that it stands above the others in my book.

449
00:32:00,970 --> 00:32:07,599
So, I was editing the audio of this video and I realized that I had completely omitted one of my

450
00:32:07,599 --> 00:32:09,839
favorite parts of this game, the side quests.

451
00:32:10,759 --> 00:32:15,700
If you've ever played a Final Fantasy game, you know that the story generally has a lull point,

452
00:32:16,119 --> 00:32:22,819
and it's a you're given somehow a means to travel around the world completing side quests that were previously unavailable.

453
00:32:23,140 --> 00:32:28,079
The cool thing about Final Fantasy VIII is that there are actually many points where this happens.

454
00:32:28,599 --> 00:32:32,200
When you get the Mobile Garden up and running throughout disc 2 and 3,

455
00:32:32,579 --> 00:32:36,380
and when you get the Ragnarok ship later in disc 3 and 4.

456
00:32:36,799 --> 00:32:38,460
The Garden allows you some freedom,

457
00:32:38,599 --> 00:32:44,380
but you still can't access areas that don't have a beach because it can't fly high enough to scale cliffs,

458
00:32:44,460 --> 00:32:44,779
I guess.

459
00:32:45,359 --> 00:32:46,680
The Ragnarok fixes this.

460
00:32:46,940 --> 00:32:51,980
But, I really didn't want to talk about the traversal here, I wanted to talk about the quests themselves.

461
00:32:52,960 --> 00:32:57,980
In the Ragnarok, if you fly out into the deep sea on the side of the world where no continents

462
00:32:57,980 --> 00:33:03,380
are visible, in the center of this area is a mysterious deep sea research base.

463
00:33:03,960 --> 00:33:06,759
When you go in, you are met with a pulsating light

464
00:33:07,140 --> 00:33:09,740
and an enigmatic voice telling you to go away.

465
00:33:09,960 --> 00:33:15,279
Eventually, you fight the GF behind this voice, which is how you get the Baha Mutt.

466
00:33:16,000 --> 00:33:19,579
But, this is only the first layer of this mystery.

467
00:33:20,099 --> 00:33:23,279
After you reach him, there's this hole where the light used to be,

468
00:33:23,700 --> 00:33:26,880
leading further down into the underwater research station.

469
00:33:27,400 --> 00:33:33,160
Down there, you're met with a puzzle where you have to use steam power to open doors to get even further down.

470
00:33:33,859 --> 00:33:36,359
But there is only so much steam to use up.

471
00:33:36,740 --> 00:33:40,400
If you do the puzzle correctly, you get into this final huge chamber.

472
00:33:40,740 --> 00:33:43,059
Remember, this is all under the ocean.

473
00:33:43,579 --> 00:33:47,339
Yet, there are these ruins here from some unknown civilization.

474
00:33:47,680 --> 00:33:52,380
Again, tying into the theme that there's so much history in this world that we're just not privy to.

475
00:33:53,460 --> 00:33:57,240
As you descend in this cavern, you're met with increasingly powerful enemies.

476
00:33:58,180 --> 00:34:00,000
But the final test is at the bottom.

477
00:34:00,660 --> 00:34:04,539
This is Ultima Weapon, the second hardest fight in the game,

478
00:34:04,779 --> 00:34:08,340
and the one that I made a guide for when I was just, I think, 12.

479
00:34:09,239 --> 00:34:14,679
And it's totally optional, totally missable unless you either use a guide or just wander

480
00:34:14,960 --> 00:34:16,019
into the middle of the ocean.

481
00:34:16,860 --> 00:34:21,820
Ultima Weapon can instantly wipe a character, and regularly wipes your entire team.

482
00:34:22,539 --> 00:34:26,300
Even if you are completely prepared, it is a really challenging fight.

483
00:34:26,719 --> 00:34:28,559
However, the reward is worth it.

484
00:34:29,300 --> 00:34:31,739
It's the final, ultimate GF, Eden,

485
00:34:32,059 --> 00:34:38,559
which is the only GF summon that can do greater than 9999 damage in a single strike,

486
00:34:39,039 --> 00:34:41,159
regularly doing over 30,000.

487
00:34:42,000 --> 00:34:45,039
That's just one of the side quests, and there are many others.

488
00:34:45,900 --> 00:34:48,079
For example, getting the GF, Odin,

489
00:34:48,219 --> 00:34:54,559
and Toneberry King requires you to find this weird diamond-shaped ruin in the overworld on the Cintra continent.

490
00:34:55,199 --> 00:34:58,420
For the former, a timer appears, and you must traverse the ruins,

491
00:34:58,760 --> 00:35:05,179
defeating the enemies along the way and solving a puzzle involving removable eyes and statues in a single code.

492
00:35:05,539 --> 00:35:11,280
For the latter, you're subjected to a grueling test of defeating many Toneberries until the King comes out to face it.

493
00:35:12,230 --> 00:35:13,559
But there are many others.

494
00:35:14,039 --> 00:35:19,699
Up on the continent of Trabia, you'll meet the Shumi village, which are the same people that Norg came from,

495
00:35:20,159 --> 00:35:21,480
and they'll have a quest for you.

496
00:35:21,920 --> 00:35:25,880
Or randomly in battles, you'll see a UFO take away the enemy,

497
00:35:26,099 --> 00:35:30,199
and eventually you find the crashed UFO and the alien that inhabited it.

498
00:35:31,559 --> 00:35:34,539
But the final side quest in the game has to be my favorite,

499
00:35:34,820 --> 00:35:38,960
and it really offers no reward outside knowing that you completed it.

500
00:35:39,840 --> 00:35:45,780
In Ultimesia's castle, in Disc 4, if you ring a bell in the chapel, you can summon Omega Weapon,

501
00:35:46,320 --> 00:35:50,420
which is basically a souped-up, re-skinned version of Ultima.

502
00:35:50,840 --> 00:35:55,219
Only this dude can wipe your entire party in a single blow if you aren't careful.

503
00:35:55,920 --> 00:35:59,000
I adore the challenge that this fight poses,

504
00:35:59,579 --> 00:36:05,460
and the real fun, outside of actually beating it, is the preparation that is required, at least for me.

505
00:36:05,900 --> 00:36:12,460
The meticulous, stat min-maxing, junctioning, weapon upgrading, etc, etc, that all leads to it.

506
00:36:12,800 --> 00:36:16,599
It's so amazing, and I honestly can't believe I forgot to talk about this at first.

507
00:36:17,019 --> 00:36:18,340
But anyway, moving on.

508
00:36:28,340 --> 00:36:32,000
A lot has been said about the draw system in Final Fantasy VIII.

509
00:36:32,539 --> 00:36:35,239
I haven't heard or read any of it, but a lot has been said.

510
00:36:35,760 --> 00:36:37,800
Personally, I really enjoy it.

511
00:36:38,579 --> 00:36:42,820
For those of you who haven't played the game, here's a quick rundown of how it works.

512
00:36:43,480 --> 00:36:45,659
Every enemy in the game carries some magic,

513
00:36:46,260 --> 00:36:49,719
and there are even spots in the world where magic flows like a spring.

514
00:36:50,320 --> 00:36:57,179
Your characters, after equipping a GF, can draw the magic into themselves and either use it or store it.

515
00:36:57,840 --> 00:37:05,059
Stored magic can be junctioned, aka assigned to your character's stats like HP, Strength, Vitality, Magic, etc.

516
00:37:05,739 --> 00:37:08,739
The stronger the magic, and the more of it your character holds,

517
00:37:09,219 --> 00:37:11,539
the higher those stats go up when you junction it.

518
00:37:12,320 --> 00:37:16,579
There are tons of little nuances to learn with the junctioning system, though, such as,

519
00:37:16,840 --> 00:37:18,980
life-giving magic is better suited to HP,

520
00:37:19,659 --> 00:37:20,800
and so, in a lot of cases,

521
00:37:21,260 --> 00:37:25,440
a stronger attack spell will be less effective than a somewhat weaker healing spell.

522
00:37:26,420 --> 00:37:28,340
The reverse is true for Strength, though.

523
00:37:28,559 --> 00:37:32,480
All the other stats have this same proclivity towards certain types of spells.

524
00:37:32,980 --> 00:37:37,920
Not only that, but junctions can also be made to increase your elemental attack and defense.

525
00:37:38,500 --> 00:37:39,460
Ditto for status effects.

526
00:37:40,280 --> 00:37:42,820
You can carry a hundred of each spell you hold,

527
00:37:43,119 --> 00:37:45,619
though you can't carry all spells at all times.

528
00:37:46,239 --> 00:37:48,340
This always leads to me, every time I'm going to be able to carry all spells,

529
00:37:48,340 --> 00:37:48,340
but I'm going to carry all spells at all times.

530
00:37:48,360 --> 00:37:53,280
I play the game, drawing one hundred of nearly every early spell I can get my hands on,

531
00:37:53,619 --> 00:37:54,599
to level up my characters.

532
00:37:55,219 --> 00:37:59,480
And though the process of drawing all the needed magic can be somewhat grueling,

533
00:37:59,860 --> 00:38:02,900
I can't really fault the game for it since it was my choice to do

534
00:38:02,900 --> 00:38:07,599
so, and nothing in the game really encourages me or nudges me to do it,

535
00:38:08,059 --> 00:38:10,780
outside the desire to become as strong as possible.

536
00:38:11,659 --> 00:38:18,320
Drawing and junctioning magic effectively can make any character a powerhouse, absorbing nearly all elemental damage.

537
00:38:18,739 --> 00:38:21,619
or having super high attack stats, or whatever.

538
00:38:22,179 --> 00:38:26,380
For this reason, there really aren't normal Final Fantasy archetypes in 8.

539
00:38:27,019 --> 00:38:31,420
Any character can fill any role given the right junctions and magic equipped.

540
00:38:31,659 --> 00:38:35,760
I think this freedom is what makes creating your team so rewarding.

541
00:38:36,320 --> 00:38:41,280
Even if, during the endgame, it comes down to just junctioning the strongest types of magic for everyone,

542
00:38:41,659 --> 00:38:45,699
the process of getting to that point takes effort and is well rewarded.

543
00:38:54,909 --> 00:38:58,300
Weapons are leveled up in a way which may seem familiar now,

544
00:38:58,599 --> 00:39:01,840
but was not normal at the time for Final Fantasy.

545
00:39:02,380 --> 00:39:08,639
Just as all monsters carry magic, they also carry items, which can be used to craft upgrades for your weapons.

546
00:39:09,159 --> 00:39:13,139
Normally you get the recipes for these upgrades through reading magazines in the game,

547
00:39:13,579 --> 00:39:15,159
but they're not required.

548
00:39:15,940 --> 00:39:18,849
You can upgrade a weapon as soon as you get the right ingredients.

549
00:39:19,719 --> 00:39:23,400
This allows for crazy amounts of freedom not seen in other games,

550
00:39:23,840 --> 00:39:29,239
such as being able to craft Squall's ultimate weapon, Lionheart, in disc 1.

551
00:39:29,719 --> 00:39:34,780
This is absolutely unheard of in any of the other mainline Final Fantasy games I've played,

552
00:39:35,239 --> 00:39:37,900
and holy crap is Squall's weapon cool.

553
00:39:38,480 --> 00:39:43,179
Impractical though it may be, a gun attached to a sword, or a sword attached to a gun,

554
00:39:43,260 --> 00:39:45,280
whichever way you slice it, is awesome.

555
00:39:45,760 --> 00:39:47,760
There's even a gameplay element to using it.

556
00:39:48,059 --> 00:39:55,280
During a normal attack, right before Squall hits the enemy, pressing R1 fires the gun and significantly increases the damage.

557
00:39:55,760 --> 00:39:56,920
It's such a simple thing,

558
00:39:57,099 --> 00:40:03,940
but that added to the active time battle version of the normal turn-based combat can make fights a lot more intense.

559
00:40:04,780 --> 00:40:09,900
And when Squall's health gets low, or the aura spell is cast, he goes into his limit break,

560
00:40:10,239 --> 00:40:15,760
which requires the player to again pull the trigger on the gunblade for every hit he performs.

561
00:40:16,179 --> 00:40:20,199
It's not just the gameplay though, just look at these fucking limit breaks.

562
00:40:30,409 --> 00:40:32,340
God damn I love this game.

563
00:40:33,199 --> 00:40:35,820
Each character has their own unique limit break too,

564
00:40:36,219 --> 00:40:38,340
and all but one of them are really awesome.

565
00:40:38,639 --> 00:40:42,460
For Irvine, you get to fire his gun, choosing different types of ammo.

566
00:40:42,639 --> 00:40:45,980
Some of them are explosive, some of them are energy rounds, etc.

567
00:40:46,780 --> 00:40:50,340
Zell's is basically like a mini fighting game, requiring a lot of damage to the enemy.

568
00:40:50,480 --> 00:40:52,460
And button combinations to perform certain moves.

569
00:40:53,340 --> 00:40:55,619
We've already talked about Quistis' blue magic,

570
00:40:56,179 --> 00:41:02,840
but Rinoa uses her arm as a cannon and fires her dog like a missile, which is fucking genius.

571
00:41:03,460 --> 00:41:07,199
Only Selfie's ability is boring, and yet it's one of the most powerful.

572
00:41:07,940 --> 00:41:10,719
It's basically just a slot machine that you keep on refreshing,

573
00:41:11,199 --> 00:41:16,199
and it can cast different magics, some of which are really powerful and completely unique to her.

574
00:41:34,739 --> 00:41:39,699
So I had to put in a little section here to showcase some of the GF summons in this game,

575
00:41:40,179 --> 00:41:43,340
because wow, they are absolutely stunning.

576
00:41:43,940 --> 00:41:45,900
There isn't a single weak one in the bunch.

577
00:41:46,500 --> 00:41:49,760
Ifrit rides a giant flaming meteor high in the air,

578
00:41:50,019 --> 00:41:50,340
and then does it.

579
00:41:50,380 --> 00:41:53,000
A back breaking move to punch it back down on the enemy.

580
00:41:53,699 --> 00:41:59,099
The brothers play a game of rock, paper, scissors to see which one gets launched up at the enemy,

581
00:41:59,500 --> 00:42:01,739
with the loser sobbing as he's flying up.

582
00:42:02,380 --> 00:42:04,260
Shiva. Oh Shiva.

583
00:42:05,059 --> 00:42:07,699
She made me feel some feelings as a young 11 year old.

584
00:42:08,199 --> 00:42:14,119
She shoots up from the ground in this icicle, breaks it apart, and sends shards hurtling at the enemy.

585
00:42:14,760 --> 00:42:17,539
Bahamut, a mainstay in the Final Fantasy series,

586
00:42:17,860 --> 00:42:23,239
is an awesome dark dragon shown that he's got him flying just under the clouds, barely peeking through,

587
00:42:23,599 --> 00:42:27,179
and then unleashes his ultimate mega flare down on the enemy.

588
00:42:27,679 --> 00:42:34,659
They're just so well animated and done with such clear love for these characters that it's a joy to summon them every time.

589
00:42:35,179 --> 00:42:38,800
But there's a lot more to the GF than just their summon attacks though.

590
00:42:39,260 --> 00:42:45,579
Each one learns different types of abilities, and when junction to a character, allows the character to use said abilities.

591
00:42:46,360 --> 00:42:50,119
Certain abilities are unique to certain GFs, which can be used to have a lot of abilities.

592
00:42:50,139 --> 00:42:53,840
They're just so much to make the character they're junction to even more like a certain archetype,

593
00:42:53,900 --> 00:42:56,920
like an attack or defense, mage or healer, whatever.

594
00:42:57,420 --> 00:43:00,719
There's more to it even than that, but I'll leave it there for now.

595
00:43:10,480 --> 00:43:14,920
Did you think that I'd talk about 8 without bringing up the OG card minigame?

596
00:43:15,519 --> 00:43:20,019
Triple Triad was Gwent, before Gwent was a twinkle in the eyes of CD Projekt.

597
00:43:20,960 --> 00:43:26,460
I have spent at least as much time playing this card game as I have playing the entire rest of

598
00:43:26,460 --> 00:43:28,980
the game, because it's just so fucking genius.

599
00:43:29,519 --> 00:43:32,719
And it's even integrated into the main game in some really cool ways.

600
00:43:33,500 --> 00:43:34,820
So basic rundown of the game.

601
00:43:35,139 --> 00:43:38,519
You start with a board with 9 spaces for cards to be placed.

602
00:43:38,960 --> 00:43:41,340
Each player takes a turn laying the card down.

603
00:43:41,760 --> 00:43:44,719
The cards have 4 numbers on them, one for each side.

604
00:43:45,260 --> 00:43:47,320
If you lay a card next to an opponent's card,

605
00:43:47,519 --> 00:43:50,360
and your card has a higher number on the sides that touch,

606
00:43:50,699 --> 00:43:53,880
then their card is flipped and is now considered yours.

607
00:43:54,400 --> 00:43:59,159
Do this until 9 spaces are filled, and whoever has the most cards on the board wins.

608
00:43:59,659 --> 00:44:00,360
Pretty simple, right?

609
00:44:00,860 --> 00:44:03,960
Well, there are a ton of confounding factors.

610
00:44:04,460 --> 00:44:07,260
Each region in the game has its own unique rule sets,

611
00:44:07,659 --> 00:44:11,420
like some cards will have elements and some spaces have elements too.

612
00:44:11,880 --> 00:44:16,139
Placing a card in that space with a matching element adds to the numbers on the card,

613
00:44:16,360 --> 00:44:17,940
or if it's not, it detracts from them.

614
00:44:18,420 --> 00:44:24,719
Other regions use the same rule, which will flip multiple cards if you match those touching numbers exactly.

615
00:44:25,559 --> 00:44:30,860
Some regions allow the winner to take one card from the loser, others allow you to take all of them.

616
00:44:31,340 --> 00:44:31,840
Stuff like that.

617
00:44:32,579 --> 00:44:35,079
Not only that, but since each region is different,

618
00:44:35,280 --> 00:44:38,519
and as you travel between them you take the rules you learned with you,

619
00:44:38,840 --> 00:44:41,280
then you mix them together with the region you're visiting.

620
00:44:41,800 --> 00:44:46,219
It just gets delightfully complex and it is hopelessly addicting.

621
00:44:47,400 --> 00:44:51,079
As I said, there are benefits to playing the game outside of winning cards.

622
00:44:51,519 --> 00:44:55,619
The GF Quetzalcoatl has two abilities, card and card mod.

623
00:44:56,280 --> 00:45:00,039
The first allows you to turn any non-boss enemy into a card.

624
00:45:00,460 --> 00:45:05,539
And the second, even better ability allows you to transform cards into useful items.

625
00:45:06,139 --> 00:45:08,480
And when I say useful, I really mean it.

626
00:45:09,019 --> 00:45:12,079
Some of these items can only be obtained through cards.

627
00:45:12,619 --> 00:45:15,019
Either that, or they have rare drop rates

628
00:45:15,280 --> 00:45:19,219
when battling monsters so card mod is the most effective way of getting them.

629
00:45:19,780 --> 00:45:22,059
You can mod cards into all kinds of items,

630
00:45:22,460 --> 00:45:28,199
from ones that can be used to refine into spells, to others that will teach your GFs really powerful abilities,

631
00:45:28,980 --> 00:45:31,840
to others that can be used straight up in upgrading your weapons.

632
00:45:32,539 --> 00:45:35,460
It's probably the single most useful ability in the game,

633
00:45:36,119 --> 00:45:38,960
and it makes playing Triple Triad all the more rewarding.

634
00:45:55,619 --> 00:46:01,960
The music in this game plays in my dreams, in my random thoughts throughout the day.

635
00:46:02,219 --> 00:46:08,699
It's been 20 years since I first heard the soundtrack, and it's still stuck in my head.

636
00:46:09,420 --> 00:46:11,500
I've been playing it in the background of this video,

637
00:46:11,800 --> 00:46:14,219
so maybe it'll be stuck in yours now too.

638
00:46:15,039 --> 00:46:21,300
I've heard the remastered versions of these songs, and while they're good, there's this charm to the heavily compressed,

639
00:46:21,480 --> 00:46:27,039
synthesized versions from the original, kind of in the same way that 8-bit music has its own charm,

640
00:46:27,239 --> 00:46:29,920
leading musicians to create new works in that genre.

641
00:46:30,719 --> 00:46:34,159
The card game tune and the battle music especially slap,

642
00:46:34,460 --> 00:46:37,539
and give an awesome added layer of tension to these moments.

643
00:46:38,079 --> 00:46:43,000
The slower songs, like the one you can hear in the concert on disc 2, are heart-wrenching,

644
00:46:43,159 --> 00:46:49,239
even with Kenny G sti- no, because of Kenny G styled synthesized saxophone.

645
00:46:49,920 --> 00:46:54,320
And then there is the absolutely haunting song, Libere Fatale,

646
00:46:54,920 --> 00:47:00,579
a Latin choral piece that adds a real sense of dread in the confrontations with the sorceresses.

647
00:47:01,159 --> 00:47:03,340
You hear this in the intro of the game as well.

648
00:47:04,000 --> 00:47:06,920
I'll often hear these songs in other YouTubers' videos,

649
00:47:07,400 --> 00:47:09,679
and yet not nobody really talks about where they're from.

650
00:47:10,199 --> 00:47:13,920
Nobuo Oemetsu, I'm really sorry if I mispronounced that name,

651
00:47:14,239 --> 00:47:17,860
but he absolutely knocked it out of the park with his soundtrack,

652
00:47:18,500 --> 00:47:21,260
and I wanted to take the time to thank him for it.

653
00:47:21,699 --> 00:47:26,119
I think he said it best when describing the music or the motivation behind creating it.

654
00:47:26,719 --> 00:47:32,440
He said, I think it will be a shame if we won't be able to cry as we play our own game.

655
00:47:33,940 --> 00:47:39,159
If you know me outside of YouTube, you know that I've suffered with depression for many years.

656
00:47:39,679 --> 00:47:40,940
If you don't, then you don't.

657
00:47:41,159 --> 00:47:43,260
This is the first time I've talked about it on the channel.

658
00:47:43,880 --> 00:47:49,179
I recently took a short break from producing videos to focus more on my mental health and to look for

659
00:47:49,179 --> 00:47:51,460
a job, as I left my PhD program.

660
00:47:52,380 --> 00:47:57,760
For some reason, though, when I'm feeling especially down, I tend to gravitate toward this game.

661
00:47:58,300 --> 00:48:00,440
Hence why I've played it so many times,

662
00:48:00,860 --> 00:48:02,980
and started without finishing even more.

663
00:48:03,820 --> 00:48:07,599
Make no mistake, I don't want to claim that depression is curable by a video game.

664
00:48:08,059 --> 00:48:12,500
It's a medical condition, a chemical imbalance in the brain that needs medicine to treat.

665
00:48:13,019 --> 00:48:20,119
Yet hearing that opening tune or starting up a game of triple triad is like an instant shot of dopamine to my brain.

666
00:48:20,599 --> 00:48:25,199
And so I will be forever grateful to the mines at Square Enix for making it.

667
00:48:25,980 --> 00:48:28,619
It may not be a cure, but it's definitely a comfort.

668
00:48:29,199 --> 00:48:32,860
One that I keep going back to time and time again for the gameplay.

669
00:48:33,480 --> 00:48:35,260
The classic, bombastic story.

670
00:48:35,639 --> 00:48:36,599
The timeless music.

671
00:48:37,300 --> 00:48:41,300
For the whole thing, which to me is greater than the sum of its parts.

672
00:48:42,079 --> 00:48:45,699
So after all that, would I recommend someone play this game?

673
00:48:46,360 --> 00:48:47,840
Well, maybe.

674
00:48:49,019 --> 00:48:52,159
There's a remastered version on Steam for PC and mobile.

675
00:48:52,699 --> 00:48:57,449
It has slightly improved graphics and is in HD, as you can see here,

676
00:48:57,760 --> 00:48:58,960
and it has some decent features.

677
00:48:59,539 --> 00:49:01,659
But for my money, the original is best.

678
00:49:01,860 --> 00:49:06,400
Granted, I have nostalgia glasses, so the graphics don't look quite as bad to me.

679
00:49:06,920 --> 00:49:11,659
All the emulator apps allow you to map special buttons like fast forwarding the game,

680
00:49:11,980 --> 00:49:15,380
which are priceless when playing it through some of the old grindier bits.

681
00:49:16,059 --> 00:49:17,860
Definitely give it a try if you haven't played it.

682
00:49:18,360 --> 00:49:21,199
If you can get past the outdated look, there's a lot to like.

683
00:49:21,599 --> 00:49:24,199
And a lot of love put into the world by its creators.

684
00:49:25,280 --> 00:49:26,900
So thank you for watching my video.

685
00:49:27,480 --> 00:49:33,019
I really appreciate that I'm able to do these and more thankful that people actually like to watch them.

686
00:49:33,280 --> 00:49:38,179
That's absolutely wild to me in a way I don't think I could ever accurately express.

687
00:49:38,699 --> 00:49:43,679
To my patrons especially, who waited patiently for whatever came next, thank you.

688
00:49:43,900 --> 00:49:49,199
Thank you for your support and for all the kind messages when I told you I needed to take a break.

689
00:49:49,539 --> 00:49:51,480
And I have some good news as well.

690
00:49:52,000 --> 00:49:56,900
I got a job as a professional tutor for physics and math, which is really awesome.

691
00:49:57,099 --> 00:50:01,519
It should allow me more freedom to continue producing content like this.

692
00:50:01,639 --> 00:50:06,619
And my ultimate goal, as you may know if you've watched these ending notes before,

693
00:50:07,099 --> 00:50:08,760
is to make this a full-time job.

694
00:50:09,440 --> 00:50:13,679
I love getting to be creative, talking about things I'm passionate about.

695
00:50:14,579 --> 00:50:18,599
So if you enjoy these videos and would like to help support me in that endeavor,

696
00:50:19,059 --> 00:50:20,440
please consider becoming a patron.

697
00:50:21,059 --> 00:50:22,159
I think that's all for now.

698
00:50:22,519 --> 00:50:24,219
Thank you and I'll see you next time.

